Reproduction check against snapshot 69 (rank, matched chunk, error, and position of every question):
  select a.q->>'id', a.q->>'rank', b.q->>'rank', a.q->>'matchedChunkId', b.q->>'matchedChunkId', a.q->>'error', b.q->>'error'
  from (select q, ord from retrieval_evaluations, jsonb_array_elements(results->'questions') with ordinality as t(q,ord) where id=69) a
  full join (select q, ord from retrieval_evaluations, jsonb_array_elements(results->'questions') with ordinality as t(q,ord) where id=91) b on a.q->>'id'=b.q->>'id'
  where a.q->>'rank' is distinct from b.q->>'rank' or a.q->>'matchedChunkId' is distinct from b.q->>'matchedChunkId' or a.q is null or b.q is null or a.ord<>b.ord;
  -> 0 rows. The aggregate columns and properties of 69 and 91 are equal (psql select of both rows). No drift.

Slice split recomputed outside the service (question text from retrieval-set-v2.json through FilingRetrievalRepository.figureTerms via jshell on target/classes; ranks from snapshot 91):
  figure (12): aapl-11 1, aapl-12 1, aapl-13 1, aapl-14 1, msft-11 1, msft-12 2, msft-13 1, msft-14 1, nvda-11 1, nvda-12 5, nvda-13 1, nvda-14 1   -> 12 of 12 at 5
  nonFigure (30): aapl-01..10 ranks 1 1 2 1 1 2 1 1 8 1; msft-01..10 ranks 6 2 2 4 2 1 7 miss 1 1; nvda-01..10 ranks 3 miss 1 miss 10 1 miss 5 miss 1   -> 21 of 30 at 5
  Not at 5 in the non-figure slice: ranked 6 to 10 aapl-09 (8), msft-01 (6), msft-07 (7), nvda-05 (10); not in the window msft-08, nvda-02, nvda-04, nvda-07, nvda-09.
  On v2 the slices are exactly the 12 questions added in v2 (-11 to -14) and the 30 carried from v1.

Floor derivation (BigDecimal, jshell): 0.700000 - 0.1 = 0.600000; / 0.05 = 12; FLOOR -> 12; x 0.05 = 0.60.
  rag.evaluation.min-non-figure-hit-at-5 = 0.60 (application.yaml, RetrievalEvaluationProperties default; RetrievalEvaluationSetTests and RetrievalEvaluationSetLoaderTests assert it).
  What it protects: 0.60 of 30 = 18 hits needed (17 of 30 = 0.566667 fails); snapshot 91 has 21, so at most 3 can be lost.
  Aggregate floor unchanged at 0.65: 28 of 42 needed; snapshot 91 has 33, so at most 5 can be lost in total. With both floors, a loss of up to 5 hits passes
  when no more than 3 of them are non-figure; the figure slice alone is guarded only by the aggregate (up to 5 of its 12 hits if the non-figure slice holds).

